      "side": 1,
      "message": "Sorry, not sure if I got your point on \"active wake mask.\". As per the LPC_HOST_EVENT_WAKE \nimplementation, I couldn\u0027t find any active wakemask (wakemask set in S0?). \nThe wake masks are set/cleared in sleep entry/exit. For example, the hostevent\nEC_CMD_HOST_EVENT_SET_WAKE_MASK (used in S3 and S5) overrides the wake mask.\nSimilar way in case of S0ix, the wake mask is overriden. Does this clarify your concern?\n\n\nPlease find the EC_CMD_HOST_EVENT_SET_WAKE_MASK code snippet below\n\nstatic int host_event_set_wake_mask(struct host_cmd_handler_args *args)\n{\n        const struct ec_params_host_event_mask *p \u003d args-\u003eparams;\n\n        lpc_set_host_event_mask(LPC_HOST_EVENT_WAKE, p-\u003emask);\n        return EC_RES_SUCCESS;\n}\nDECLARE_HOST_COMMAND(EC_CMD_HOST_EVENT_SET_WAKE_MASK,\n                     host_event_set_wake_mask,\n                     EC_VER_MASK(0));",
      "parentUuid": "96b9da7e_5e2e1c8b",
